[#:seon.task{:name "open-tasks-with-all-proofs-green-are-not-flagged"
             :intent "Every bucket-D task in tmp/orchestrator/triage.tsv whose proofs were checked on 2026-10-07 has all proofs green while the task stays open: seon.call-preparation/acquired-functions-get-no-supplied-defaults (2 proofs), seon.fn/host-bound-class-list-copies-interpreter-config, seon.sci.eval/program-change-check-scans-the-whole-history, seon.render/a-renderer-is-chosen-by-key-presence (2 proofs), seon.db/the-query-wrapper-costs-36x-datahike and seon.repl/reply-map-is-not-edn-when-elided-or-rendered (`my.test/check` on branch agent ctx-ex-1 and recorded results on default). Either the work is done and the task should close, or the proof does not test the intent (e.g. seon.db/the-query-wrapper-costs-36x-datahike's intent is a 36x cost, its proof bounds armed work). A green proof on an open task must be visible in the task's view and in the queue, and a task's proof must fail before its fix. Measured again by root on 2026-10-09 (default e9582ffc7, then c7a7030d8 after the 114-task retirement): of 74 then 51 open tasks with tagged proofs, 67 proofs and then every proof of 24 tasks ran green, among them `seon.error/an-unresolved-symbol-shows-an-empty-neighbour-list`, `my.program/source-shows-code-as-an-escaped-string` and seven `seon.bootstrap/help-*` tasks, so the open list is mostly finished work and picking a red task costs a test run per candidate. A task whose every proof is green is done (`seon.context/task-done?`): ingestion or `bin/lane commit` reports each such task on the committed program, and the finished entries are retired."
             :must-read #{seon.task/task-edges seon.test/recorded-result seon.context/task-done? seon.task/assign!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/context-examples/README.md"}}
#:seon.task{:name "tasks-have-no-done-when-and-name-subjects-only-through-must-read"
             :intent "`seon.task/task-edges` answers :subjects #{} for most tasks: the functions a task is about are on the task's `:seon.task/must-read`, not on the functions' :seon/tasks. Context assembly from the proc transcript (S4) must union both. No :seon.task/done-when exists; under the 2026-10-07 ruling done = the proofs green, so a task without proofs cannot be launched: refuse assignment of a task with no proof test."
             :must-read #{seon.task/task-edges seon.task/assign!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/context-examples/README.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "task-text-references-are-never-resolved",
            :intent
            "Over the 392 tasks installed on default: `:seon.task/must-read` names 41 symbols that resolve to no function, test or namespace (e.g. seon.print.value/bounded-text, seon.cluster/mcp-get-value, my.program/overrides); intents name 44 qualified symbols, 42 qualified keywords and about 34 namespaces that resolve to nothing (e.g. :seon.issue/id, :seon.task/done-when, my.plan). `seon.task/task-findings` checks only :seon/tasks tags. A task brief built from references shows a dangling reference as a hole. Done when task ingestion reports dangling must-read symbols per task (the program gate refusing new ones) and intent references are resolved by the same reference index, with counts in the notes.",
            :must-read #{seon.task/task-findings},
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/context-design/reference-kinds-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-runtime-created-task-is-never-written-back"
  :intent "A task made by `seon.task/create!` exists only in the database: a deftest tagged :seon/tasks with its ns/name is refused at publication as a dangling id, and a reset loses it. Lanes hand-copied 8+ tasks into resources/seon/tasks on 2026-10-08. CLAUDE.md: \"Files are the write-back of accepted entities.\" Correct: the task's home write-back stages the accepted task into resources/seon/tasks/<ns>.edn like any accepted entity, and ingesting that file entry over the runtime row yields one task (see a-file-task-is-refused-while-a-runtime-task-holds-its-symbol). Proof: create! then write-back produces the EDN entry, and a deftest tagged with the new task publishes without a dangling-id refusal."
  :must-read #{seon.task/create! seon.task/index-tasks!}
  :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/split/reconciled-plan.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "assign-cannot-see-a-red-proof-the-gate-will-not-land"
             :intent "`seon.task/assign!` reads proofs from the home database only, and a proof reaches the home only by commit and a restart of default, while a throwaway check refuses a commit whose named test is red (`bin/lane commit --branch-evidence` now has `--accept-red-before`). So root cannot assign a task whose red proof exists only on a branch. Its refusal \"seon.task is refused: no-proofs.\" names neither the task nor the fix. Done when root can assign a task whose red proof exists on the agent's branch or in an accepted-red commit, and the refusal names the task and the `:seon/tasks` tag to add."
             :must-read #{seon.task/assign! seon.task/task-edges}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/dogfood/pilot.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-assignment-reads-only-its-proofs"
             :intent "One `seon.task/assign!` allocated 64.4 MB in 1,407 armed calls and 62 ms on the cluster: `seon.task/task-edges` runs two `or` queries (holders, referrers) and assign! needs only the proofs. A proof is one indexed query from the task's tag; the assignment read allocates under 8 MB. The proof is not yet trustworthy: at default bb934b396 (2026-10-09, fresh store) it measured 11,681,312 bytes red on main, then went green on fan-out 8 agent fan8-assign's branch, which evaluated only `in-ns` and two `my.program/source` reads and changed nothing; an allocation bound whose outcome depends on the branch or cache state it runs from proves nothing about a fix, so the proof measures what the assignment read itself allocates, the same on every branch for an unchanged program: `seon.task/assignment-read`; `seon.task/assign!` runs no proof (the agent's first pass proves, `seon.turn/prove-turn`)."
             :must-read #{seon.task/assign! seon.task/assignment-read seon.task/task-edges}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/schedule/agent-loop-ledger.md#LR-ASSIGNWRITER"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-task-evidence-path-names-no-gitignored-file"
             :intent "AGENTS.md: task evidence never points into gitignored `tmp/`. The census `seon.task-ingestion-test/a-task-evidence-path-names-no-gitignored-file` reads every `:seon.task/evidence` path in resources/seon/tasks and lists those under a directory `.gitignore` names. Red at 4027882d4 with two tasks in seon.turn.edn (their paths now point at the committed copies under docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence) and one that remains, `seon.fn.analyzer/local-root-dependency-analysis-goes-stale`, naming a data/ log. Done when the census answers [] and task ingestion reports an evidence path under an ignored directory as a problem on the task."
             :must-read #{seon.task/index-tasks! seon.task/task-files}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-10/laws-without-proofs.md"}} #:seon.task{:name "an-ended-summary-survives-retiring-its-branch"
             :intent "`seon.context/ended` derived an ended task's calls, tokens and proofs from the agent's branch, so once the branch was retired it reported zero calls and tokens and omitted the proofs (astra day audit finding 8). Done when the small historical outcome (`:seon.task/calls`, `:seon.task/prompt-tokens`, `:seon.task/completion-tokens`, `:seon.task/proof-counts`, `:seon.task/red-proofs`) is recorded as `:seon.agent/outcome` on the ending agent at the writer when the task ends, `seon.context/ended` reads it when the branch is gone, and when neither the branch nor the record remains the summary carries `:seon.task/end-unknown` and no zero counts."
             :must-read #{seon.context/ended seon.turn/end-task-call seon.turn/end-task!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-10/astra-day-audit.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-needs-cycle-is-refused-at-the-writer"
             :intent "Card S1. Schema: `:seon.task/children` (component ref set of child tasks), `:seon.task/needs` (indexed ref set), `:seon.task/instructions`, `:seon.task/execution` (`:seon.wake/starts true`), `:seon.task/cron`, `:seon.task/zone`, `:seon.task/function`, the attempt facts on the assignment row (`:seon.task/attempt-of`, `:seon.task.attempt/end`, `:seon.task.attempt/target`, `:seon.task.attempt/reason`, `:seon.task.attempt/commit`) and the firing (`:seon.task.fire/id`, `:seon.task.fire/at`, `:seon.task.fire/of`, `:seon.task.fire/to`); task EDN authors children and needs as lookup refs; the writer refuses a needs cycle (`seon.task/refuse-needs-cycle`, called by `seon.task/create!` and `seon.task/index-tasks!`); adoption proven on a branch of the live store."
             :must-read #{seon.task/create! seon.task/index-tasks! seon.cluster.wake/starting-attributes}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/runtime-follows-db.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-ready-leaves-are-those-whose-needs-are-done"
             :intent "Card S2 (`seon.task/ready` answers the handles that should run now over a database value as two `seon.db/q` reads with `seon.task/ready-rules`, the eligible leaves minus `blocked`, evaluated unbound; `seon.task/done?`; `seon.task/resolution`; proof: P1's twelve scenarios on the fifty-leaf tree and the ready read under 10 ms through `seon.profile/measure`). (hybrid-done-and-merge M8, reused) `leaf-done` in `seon.task/ready-rules` and `seon.task/done?` read 'the latest assignment of the leaf has `:seon.task/outcome` `:merged`' instead of an assignment's `:done` end; the scenarios and the cost bound survive."
             :must-read #{seon.task/ready seon.task/ready-rules seon.task/done? seon.task/resolution seon.db/q seon.profile/measure}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-done-and-merge.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-attempt-is-written-once-with-its-agent"
             :intent "Card S3, slice 1. `seon.task/attempt-tx` answers the attempt row of task `handle` for `agent-id` on `branch`: `:seon.task/assignment` is `seon.id/id [handle n]` where `:seon.task.attempt/number` n is one more than the task's ended attempts, with `:seon.task/attempt-of` beside the handle value; the caller concatenates the agent's creation (`seon.cluster.agent/creation-tx`) so both are one transaction on main; an open attempt already written answers [], so a second write writes nothing. `seon.task/assign!` writes its row through it."
             :must-read #{seon.task/attempt-tx seon.task/assign! seon.cluster.agent/creation-tx seon.id/id}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/r1-db-flow-design.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/runtime-follows-db.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-sent-back-end-reopens-its-target"
             :intent "Card S4. `seon.turn/end-task-call` records :sent-back with `:seon.task/target` and the decision in the attempt's one end transaction; `seon.task/done` honors it (the target is no longer done, its successors stop being ready). A row in the S2 table."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/end-task-call seon.turn/task-end}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/runtime-follows-db.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-repeated-problem-writes-nothing"
             :intent "Card Q1. A problem task is created by identity `seon.id/id [class subject]` with its instructions as data on the task, assigned to root (or to a fresh agent for error signatures and cost regressions); writing the same problem twice writes nothing; the merge request a green end records becomes one problem class (runtime-follows-db §5)."
             :must-read #{seon.id/id seon.task/create!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/runtime-follows-db.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "each-problem-class-is-detected-from-its-facts"
             :intent "Card Q2. Each problem class of runtime-follows-db §5 (an end other than done; a send-back loop; a stuck chain; observed not matching intent; a stale heartbeat; refused delivery; an unresolved reference; an error signature; a cost regression) is detected in the pass that already sees its facts (the reconciler's, the heartbeat's, or a listened fact) and creates its problem task; one table row per class, two classes per lane."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/task-end seon.cluster.wake/delivery seon.health/report}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/runtime-follows-db.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-refinement-on-a-branch-reaches-main-only-at-the-end"
             :intent "Phase AW4 of hybrid-agent-world.md (after AW0; beside AW3 and AW5 by file). The task-home lookups (main, main-connection in seon.task) are deleted (AW4 slice 2); `seon.task/written`, `assign!` and `adopt-tasks-tx` transact on the connection they are given; `seon.context/held-task`, `ended`, `end-summary-tx` and `current-state` read the world's database only (the branch holds its task and attempt because it forked from the main commit that wrote them); `seon.turn/admission-closed?`, `task-end`, `end-message`, `next-agent-work` and `task-proofs` lose every (task/main database) read; :seon.agent/admission-closed-tx writes go (the end on the attempt is the fact). Proof: this test (an agent's `my.task/refine!` on its branch leaves main's intent unchanged while the attempt runs and equal after the end copy; a root edit of the same attribute meanwhile keeps root's value on main and writes exactly one problem task); seon.profile/calls-of of seon.task/main is zero because it no longer exists. Files: src/seon/task.clj, src/seon/context.clj, src/seon/turn.clj (remaining reads), test/seon/task_test.clj."
             :must-read #{seon.task/attempt-rows-tx seon.task/create! seon.task/assign! seon.task/adopt-tasks-tx seon.context/held-task seon.context/end-summary-tx seon.turn/task-end}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/hybrid-agent-world.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-step-selects-its-obligations-by-its-kind"
  :intent "Phase P2 of hybrid-step-semantics.md (platform slice). The step kind is one fact on the task: `:seon.task/step` [:enum :prove :implement] on `:seon.task/task` (absent reads :implement; vocabulary row under 'subject, step'); `:seon.task.attempt/end` gains :error; `:seon.task.attempt/relaunch` (root's reason on an ended attempt) with optional `:seon.task.attempt/relaunch-fork` (the commit attempt n+1 forks instead of the ended attempt's fork point); `:seon.error/unimplemented`, the variant Design's contracted stubs fail with. One selector, `seon.task/obligations` (database, task-sym) -> {:seon.task/step k :seon.task/proofs own tagged deftests :seon.task/product deftests tagged with the tasks whose :seon.task/needs name this one}, two reads over :seon.task/tasks, replaces every other reader of a step's proofs: `seon.task/assign!`'s refusal, the test step (`seon.turn/task-proofs` goes), `seon.context/proofs`, `seon.context/task-done?`'s own selection, `seon.turn/task-end` and `seon.cluster.agent/plan-facts`' validity. Proof: seon.task-test/obligations-select-by-step (table: implement; prove with dependents; prove with own proofs; absent step = implement). Files: resources/seon/schemas/seon.task.edn, seon.task.attempt.edn, seon.error.edn, docs/seon/architecture/vocabulary.md, src/seon/task.clj, test/seon/task_test.clj."
  :must-read #{seon.task/task-edges seon.task/assign! seon.turn/task-proofs seon.context/task-done? seon.context/proofs seon.cluster.agent/plan-facts}
  :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-step-semantics.md"}}]
